{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"mandated-status-surface-omitted","classStatement":"The CLI criterion does not cover the mandated status surface.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC12 (lines 121–127) specifies `gatereeve metrics convergence` but no change to `gatereeve status`; supplied decision D9 says status is unchanged.","failureScenario":"A user opens `gatereeve status` for the #149 metrics -> the four measures are absent from the CLI status surface named in the mandate.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"projection-text-contradiction","classStatement":"The escaped-defect criterion contradicts the design’s projection limit.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC8 (lines 97–103) requires projecting escaped-defect links and a human basis. requirements/design.md line 54 says text beyond the bounded class statement is never projected; the supplied D4 decision describes the links and basis as free-form.","failureScenario":"A confirmed defect has a finding link -> projecting its free-form basis violates the approved design, while omitting the link prevents the store-only measure from counting the defect.","id":"F2","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"fallback-dependency-blocks-docs","classStatement":"The issue dependencies prevent the mandated desktop fallback from delivering documentation.","document":"requirements/issues.md","evidence":"I-3 (lines 32–41) combines CLI and desktop work; I-4 (lines 43–52), which delivers the user guide, depends on I-3. Spec AC13 (lines 131–134) permits leaving desktop open while AC14 documentation still applies.","failureScenario":"Desktop work proves much larger and is left open as mandated -> I-3 cannot finish, so its dependency holds I-4 and the required user guide remains undelivered.","id":"F3","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"fallback-rubric-evidence-gap","classStatement":"The desktop rubric omits evidence for its permitted fallback.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"Rubric R13 (line 156) allows a spec amendment and #149 comment as its fallback pass condition, but its Evidence column lists only `apps/desktop/test/`.","failureScenario":"Desktop is deferred -> the listed test evidence cannot establish that the amendment and issue comment exist, leaving the alternate pass condition without specified review evidence.","id":"F4","severity":"medium"}],"mandateAssessment":{"evidence":"The grant requires a CLI status surface. The supplied D9 decision explicitly leaves `gatereeve status` unchanged, and requirements/spec.md AC12 specifies only `gatereeve metrics convergence`. The proposed criteria therefore do not establish delivery of the named status surface.","outcome":"FAIL"},"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"Implementation should not be authorized yet. The spec omits the mandated CLI status surface and conflicts with the design’s projection limit. The plan also blocks the required user guide under the permitted desktop fallback."}